# The three homepages (root, es, zh) canonicalize to a bare trailing slash
# (see R/build_hreflang.R), but Quarto still writes and links to index.html
# with no redirect enforcing that, so Google was indexing /index.html as a
# separate, non-canonical duplicate of /. Force (!) is required here because
# these paths exactly match real files in public/, which Netlify would
# otherwise serve directly instead of applying the redirect.
/index.html / 301!
/es/index.html /es/ 301!
/zh/index.html /zh/ 301!
